# District-ready UX

Causey is for school districts, schools, coaches, parents, and students. Every change should make the full workflow more intuitive — not more enterprise-looking.

## Non-negotiables
- **Simple by default, powerful on demand.** Progressive disclosure by role.
- One dominant next action per view. Plain-language labels. No database jargon.
- Guided flows over giant forms (create → preview → publish; invite → claim).
- Preserve context: drafts, success states with next step, undo/confirm for destructive actions.
- Follow `causey-ui` / design system / anti-vibecode. No fake polish badges.

## Role landings (what each person needs first)
- Student: discover → track/register → reminders → my orgs
- Parent: which child needs action, and what kind
- Coach: tournaments, groups, invites, attendance
- Org admin: staff, settings, exports (+ coach tasks)
- District admin: schools, provisioning, aggregate reporting
- Platform admin: separate `/admin` moderation shell

## Improvement-loop rules
- Work on `dev` only unless the user says otherwise. Never merge to `main` unprompted.
- One focused, shippable UX win per iteration. Prefer end-to-end workflow fixes over cosmetic tweaks.
- Update `.cursor/district-ux-progress.md` after each change.
- Commit on `dev` with a clear why-focused message; push `dev` if tracking is set. Do not push/merge `main` unless asked.
- Prefer reuse of existing components/tokens. Do not invent new scrape paths or fabricate data.
